No users, no Unix sockets, no resource limits (docs/gpu3d.md G1).

- Kosmos has no users and no password database: `~user` is left as it
  is written, and a home is what HOME says or none;
- one machine and no sessions: a lock file's owner is "localhost", and a
  stale one is conservatively taken as still held, as on a system that
  cannot tell;
- a file system's statvfs has no flags, so whether it is local is
  answered conservatively, no, as on z/OS;
- an image is not a file a process can name, so the main executable's
  path is empty;
- no Unix domain sockets: a process speaks through endpoints it was
  handed, so raw_socket_stream is left out;
- no rlimits: the default stack size is LLVM's own 8 MB.

